    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>An island kingdom united by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamehameha-i">Kamehameha I</a> between 1795 and 1810, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lahaina">Lahaina</a> from 1820 and at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honolulu">Honolulu</a> from 1845.</li><li>It became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitutional-monarchy">constitutional monarchy</a> in 1840, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> recognised its independence in 1843.</li><li>Planters forced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayonet-constitution">Bayonet Constitution</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalakaua">Kalākaua</a> in 1887, and a committee backed by US troops overthrew Liliʻuokalani in 1893.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iolani-palace">ʻIolani Palace</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honolulu">Honolulu</a> was lit by electricity by 1887, four years before electric lighting was installed in the White House in Washington in 1891.</p></aside>
    </section>

